Template: echo-os/title
Type: title
Description: Echo OS

Template: echo-os/welcome
Type: note
Description: Welcome to Echo OS
 Echo OS starts as a headless NAS with a browser interface and proven storage
 components such as ZFS and Samba. A local HDMI desktop is an optional image
 build profile. Answer a few questions to begin the installation.

Template: echo-os/disk
Type: select
Choices: ${CHOICES}
Description: Select the system disk
 The selected disk will be used entirely for Echo OS. An SSD is recommended.
 Leave data disks unselected; storage pools can be created after installation.

Template: echo-os/confirm
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Erase ${DEVICE} and install Echo OS?
 All data on this disk will be permanently removed.

Template: echo-os/hostname
Type: string
Default: echo
Description: Device name
 This hostname identifies the NAS on your local network, for example echo.local.

Template: echo-os/password
Type: password
Description: Administrator password
 The administrator username is echo. Use at least 8 characters.

Template: echo-os/password-again
Type: password
Description: Confirm the administrator password
 Enter the same password again.

Template: echo-os/error
Type: error
Description: ${MESSAGE}
